WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.335
 Tony, Colin, congratulations.

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:03.937
The two of you
are moving forward

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:05.438
to the third and final
round of this competition.

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:06.806
Now, in this last
round, we're going

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:08.007
to send you back
to your home forges

00:00:08.107 --> 00:00:10.744
to build an iconic
weapon from history.

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:15.415
Gentlemen, we want
you to build this.

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:16.515
The Burmese dha.

00:00:16.582 --> 00:00:17.283
 Holy moly.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.919
 Hell yeah.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:21.988
NARRATOR: The Burmese
dha traces its roots back

00:00:22.054 --> 00:00:24.657
to 16th century southeast Asia.

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:27.059
The single edged, double
handed sword features

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:28.627
a slightly curved
blade, designed

00:00:28.694 --> 00:00:32.799
to inflict deep deadly, slashes
against enemies in battle.

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:34.400
The weapon was so
effective, soldiers

00:00:34.466 --> 00:00:37.637
continued to use it in combat
through World War II, where

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:40.640
US-aided resistance forces,
known as Kachin Rangers,

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:43.843
wielded this blade fighting
in the hills of Myanmar.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:45.244
 Bladesmiths,
you guys will have

00:00:45.344 --> 00:00:47.881
four days to build your
Burmese dhas, so good luck.

00:00:47.981 --> 00:00:49.149
We'll see you then.

00:00:53.085 --> 00:00:54.053
 My name is Tony Bravo.

00:00:54.153 --> 00:00:55.588 line:14%
I'm 46 years old.

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:58.391 line:8%
I'm a journeyman lineman,
and a part time bladesmith.

00:00:58.458 --> 00:01:01.160
Back home, I have a lot
of people rooting for me.

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:02.728
I've got two daughters.

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:06.665
My youngest is going off to
college, so those $10,000

00:01:06.765 --> 00:01:08.134
would definitely come in handy.

00:01:08.201 --> 00:01:09.969
This is a timed
competition, so you

00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:11.805
want to make sure that
everything sticks,

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:13.039
and you've got a
solid piece of steel.

00:01:13.105 --> 00:01:16.542
We have a heat treated
and tempered blade,

00:01:16.642 --> 00:01:19.378 line:8%
and now I'm going
to blue the spine

00:01:19.478 --> 00:01:21.547 line:14%
to give it some more durability.

00:01:21.647 --> 00:01:23.183 line:8%
Yeah, I'm starting
to see some color.

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:24.383
We're getting there.

00:01:24.483 --> 00:01:26.285
So by keeping the
blade in the wet sand,

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:28.154
it's going to act
as an insulator,

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:31.124
and it's going to prevent
the heat from traveling down.

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:32.358
Little by little.

00:01:32.424 --> 00:01:33.860
If I do it right,
I'm going to have

00:01:33.926 --> 00:01:37.763
a shock-absorbing spine that
will withstand any type of test

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:39.198
that they put on it.

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:43.135
I chose to go with Osage
orange on my handle material

00:01:43.202 --> 00:01:45.538
because it's a hard wood.

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:48.908
It'll survive any blow that
they're going to give it.

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:50.076
Everything is good.

00:01:50.142 --> 00:01:52.945
I got it fitted, it looks great.

00:01:53.011 --> 00:01:54.247
It's going to do some damage.

00:01:56.482 --> 00:01:57.049
[bleep]

00:01:57.149 --> 00:01:58.518
I almost hit the ground.

00:01:58.618 --> 00:02:00.587
[laughter]

00:02:03.889 --> 00:02:05.324
 My name is Colin Roy.

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:08.160 line:8%
I'm 28, and I'm
a full time metal

00:02:08.227 --> 00:02:09.428 line:14%
fabricator and blacksmith.

00:02:09.528 --> 00:02:11.397
Started in my parents'
one car garage.

00:02:11.463 --> 00:02:14.667
I almost burned it down
twice, but I finally saved up

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:16.970
enough money, I was able
to build my own shop,

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:18.605
and that's where I'm
working out of today.

00:02:18.705 --> 00:02:19.972
I'm way ahead of schedule.

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:22.041
I can get the blade
quenched today.

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:24.009
All right, I think
we're going for it.

00:02:24.109 --> 00:02:25.845
It's now or never.

00:02:25.912 --> 00:02:29.415
I feel my whole body tense
up as I dunk it in the oil.

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:32.952
Yep, we're good.

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:34.821
That looks [bleep] cool.

00:02:34.888 --> 00:02:37.890
I want to keep the
momentum going.

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:39.091
And that's when I see it.

00:02:39.158 --> 00:02:42.462
I got a real big
warp in the blade.

00:02:42.529 --> 00:02:44.630
Aw, that sucks.

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:46.899
It's a bit of a corkscrew,
and that's something

00:02:46.999 --> 00:02:48.234
I can't bend or grind out.

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:51.237
Looks like I'm going to
have to re-quench my blade.

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:55.174
I am dreading having
to quench again.

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:56.376
See what happens.

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:00.413
Blade goes in the oil--

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:01.313
woo!

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:05.685
Comes out, I get
it clamped down.

00:03:05.751 --> 00:03:08.755
Looks like I got the
warp almost out of it.

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:11.057
It looks good enough for now.

00:03:11.157 --> 00:03:12.858
I think we're good.

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:14.226
That is perfect.

00:03:14.327 --> 00:03:16.128
I get my handles
all fit together.

00:03:16.195 --> 00:03:17.663
Everything's
looking really good,

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:20.399
and I spend a lot of time
polishing everything, getting

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:22.301
a really nice finish on it.

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:24.737
This is one of the best
places I've ever made.

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:26.606
In my mind, this is
a winning weapon.

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:29.108
Tony, I'll see you
at the competition.

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:31.110
Better bring your A game.

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:34.379
 Bladesmiths, welcome
to the kill test.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:37.283
Your Burmese dhas
are beautiful--

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:38.918
but are they deadly?

00:03:38.985 --> 00:03:40.553
To find that out, I'm
going to take your weapons

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:44.056
and deliver some lethal
blows on this pig carcass.

00:03:44.123 --> 00:03:44.890
Tony, you're up first.

00:03:44.957 --> 00:03:45.891
You ready for this?

00:03:45.958 --> 00:03:46.725
 Absolutely.

00:03:46.792 --> 00:03:47.426
 All right.

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:49.761
So am I. Let's do this.

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:53.499
[music playing]

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:08.748
All right, Tony, let's talk
about your weapon here.

00:04:08.815 --> 00:04:11.016
This is a gorgeous piece.

00:04:11.083 --> 00:04:13.552
The handle construction, for me,
is a little bit on the larger

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:17.422
side, but every
cut, every thrust

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:19.458
is very sharp on
this pig carcass.

00:04:19.558 --> 00:04:22.928
And overall, sir,
your Burmese dha--

00:04:23.029 --> 00:04:24.530
it will kill.

00:04:24.631 --> 00:04:25.430
 Thank you, sir.

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:26.332
 All right Colin,
your turn, sir.

00:04:26.399 --> 00:04:27.299
You ready?
- Yep.

00:04:27.366 --> 00:04:29.535
 All right, let's do this.

00:04:29.636 --> 00:04:32.272
[music playing]

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:42.949
 Aw, come on.

00:04:45.317 --> 00:04:48.487
 That was a big slice.

00:04:48.587 --> 00:04:51.123
 All right, Colin, let's
talk about your weapon here.

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:52.958
Stunningly beautiful.

00:04:53.025 --> 00:04:54.327
Damascus [inaudible].

00:04:54.393 --> 00:04:55.828
Beautiful handle.

00:04:55.894 --> 00:04:58.130
Easier to control, because
it's a little bit smaller.

00:04:58.196 --> 00:05:00.366
Now, your edge is very sharp.

00:05:00.433 --> 00:05:03.269
Your tip thrusts
and slashes nicely.

00:05:03.336 --> 00:05:06.438
But you already had a little
bit of a warp earlier--

00:05:06.538 --> 00:05:10.009
now it's even more pronounced.

00:05:10.075 --> 00:05:12.979
But overall, sir, your weapon--

00:05:13.046 --> 00:05:14.112
it will kill.

00:05:14.179 --> 00:05:14.914
 Hell yeah.

00:05:17.783 --> 00:05:21.321
 Bladesmiths, welcome
to our strength test.

00:05:21.387 --> 00:05:24.590
Now I'm going to take your
beautiful Damascus swords

00:05:24.657 --> 00:05:27.359
and beat the heck out of
them against these guys

00:05:27.459 --> 00:05:29.128
in the armor, and
shields, and helmets.

00:05:29.228 --> 00:05:31.397
Now, what your blades
do to these dummies

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:33.032
is not as important
to me as what

00:05:33.098 --> 00:05:34.767
the dummies do to your blades.

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:36.135
Tony, you're up first.

00:05:36.202 --> 00:05:36.868
 Ready to go?

00:05:36.969 --> 00:05:37.869
 Get you some.

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:39.305
 I can do that.

00:05:39.405 --> 00:05:42.641
 Definitely worried
about that initial impact.

00:05:42.741 --> 00:05:44.443
They're trying to
break your blade.

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:47.613
It could be disastrous.

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:49.147
 [grunting]

00:05:49.248 --> 00:05:52.485
[music playing]

00:05:58.257 --> 00:05:59.024
All right, Tony.

00:05:59.124 --> 00:06:00.827
Breathe.

00:06:00.893 --> 00:06:01.861
This held up well.

00:06:01.927 --> 00:06:04.563
You do have a little
glinting here and there,

00:06:04.663 --> 00:06:08.901
but compared to what was
done to that, that's great.

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:10.103
Bladw'a still straight.

00:06:10.169 --> 00:06:12.638
Everything else is
still razor sharp.

00:06:12.738 --> 00:06:13.272
Good job.

00:06:13.338 --> 00:06:14.840
 Hot diggity dog.

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:15.908
 All right, Colin.

00:06:16.008 --> 00:06:17.043
How you feeling, bud?

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:19.011
 Well, we'll know
when it's done.

00:06:19.078 --> 00:06:20.146
 Well, let's find out, then.

00:06:24.383 --> 00:06:27.919
 Here we go.

00:06:27.986 --> 00:06:30.188
 [grunting]

00:06:30.289 --> 00:06:33.893
[music playing]

00:06:38.197 --> 00:06:39.465
Colin, you survived.

00:06:39.532 --> 00:06:41.401
I'm gonna start
with your handle.

00:06:41.467 --> 00:06:44.236
The smaller diameter gives
me a little more control,

00:06:44.302 --> 00:06:46.204
a little easier to hold onto.

00:06:46.271 --> 00:06:48.174
But counterbalance is nice.

00:06:48.274 --> 00:06:50.175
We've got some minor
glinting, but you've

00:06:50.275 --> 00:06:51.443
still got a good edge on there.

00:06:51.543 --> 00:06:54.046
It's still sharp, so
, overall nice job.

00:06:54.146 --> 00:06:54.947
 Thank you.

00:06:58.183 --> 00:06:59.518
 All right, bladesmiths.

00:06:59.585 --> 00:07:02.321
This is the sharpness
test, the tatami mat slice.

00:07:02.388 --> 00:07:04.089
I'm going to take
your weapon and try

00:07:04.156 --> 00:07:06.225
to across these tatami mats.

00:07:06.292 --> 00:07:07.092
Tony, you're up first.

00:07:07.159 --> 00:07:07.893
You ready for this?

00:07:07.993 --> 00:07:08.460
 Let's do it, sir.

00:07:08.527 --> 00:07:10.863
Let's do it.

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:14.934
[music playing]

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:31.017
 All right, right, Tony, let's
talk about your weapon here.

00:07:31.083 --> 00:07:33.385
Your edge does cut very well.

00:07:33.452 --> 00:07:35.253
Overall, sir, your weapon--

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:36.722
it will cut.

00:07:36.789 --> 00:07:37.790
 Thank you.

00:07:37.857 --> 00:07:39.258
 Colin, your turn, sir.
You ready?

00:07:39.358 --> 00:07:39.958
 Yep.

00:07:40.058 --> 00:07:40.760
Let's do it.

00:07:40.827 --> 00:07:43.395
 Let's do it.

00:07:43.462 --> 00:07:46.599
[music playing]

00:07:59.645 --> 00:08:01.847
All right, Colin, let's
talk about your weapon here.

00:08:01.914 --> 00:08:06.885
When the edges make contact with
the tatami mats, it will cut.

00:08:06.952 --> 00:08:09.288
 Thank you.

00:08:09.355 --> 00:08:10.689
 All right guys,
your Burmese dhas

00:08:10.756 --> 00:08:12.958
show that you are both
very skilled bladesmiths,

00:08:13.058 --> 00:08:14.760
but the judges have decided
who the "Forged in Fire"

00:08:14.826 --> 00:08:18.764
champion is, and
today that smith is--

00:08:21.266 --> 00:08:22.034
Tony.

00:08:22.101 --> 00:08:23.503
Congratulations.

00:08:23.603 --> 00:08:25.271
Now, Colin, you crushed it,
but unfortunately, you're

00:08:25.371 --> 00:08:26.739
not the "Forged in
Fire" champion today,

00:08:26.839 --> 00:08:28.741
and Doug's going
to tell you why.

00:08:28.807 --> 00:08:31.410
 Colin, you brought
us a beautiful weapon,

00:08:31.477 --> 00:08:32.912
but your weapon was
the only one that

00:08:32.978 --> 00:08:35.081
took some damage
during the kill test,

00:08:35.147 --> 00:08:36.315
where you developed the warp.

00:08:36.382 --> 00:08:37.783
That's the reason
you didn't win today.

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:39.151
 Understood.

00:08:39.217 --> 00:08:41.487
 Well, Colin, unfortunately,
your time in this competition

00:08:41.587 --> 00:08:42.688
has ended.

00:08:42.788 --> 00:08:44.290
I'm gonna have to
ask you to please

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:45.423
step off the Forged floor, but
thank you for your hard work.

00:08:45.490 --> 00:08:46.592
 Thank you.

00:08:46.692 --> 00:08:48.227
I'm really disappointed
that I'm getting

00:08:48.293 --> 00:08:50.596
sent home for that stupid warp.

00:08:50.696 --> 00:08:52.598
I should have just
made a new blade.

00:08:52.698 --> 00:08:54.534
But it was a real
close competition.

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:57.369
If I'm going to lose to
someone, I'm glad it was Tony.

00:08:57.436 --> 00:08:58.304
[bleep] warps.

00:09:01.006 --> 00:09:03.409
 Well, Tony, it was not an
easy road, but you did it.

00:09:03.476 --> 00:09:04.777
You are the newest
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:09:04.843 --> 00:09:07.212
You just won yourself
a check for $10,000.

00:09:07.313 --> 00:09:08.080
Congratulations.

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:09.348
 Woo!

00:09:09.448 --> 00:09:12.351
 This challenge
really made me realize,

00:09:12.451 --> 00:09:14.252
whatever you want to
do, go out and do it.

00:09:14.319 --> 00:09:16.055
Just be the best at it.

00:09:16.155 --> 00:09:20.326
My name is Tony, and I am the
"Forged in Fire" champion.

